coverage.json records every upstream guide and every one of the 39 algorithm
module paths and source hashes. The 66 native Skills are adapted operational
instructions, not unmodified copies of the upstream execution policy.

Local modifications:
  Replaced UnitaryLab runtime dependencies with Qiskit, PennyLane, NumPy, SciPy,
  Qiskit Algorithms, PySCF and quimb. Kept explicit circuits, oracles, finite-Fock
  optical layers, binary code construction and the stated numerical methods.
  CVQNN's optical layer follows the MIT CVSimulator/CVClassifier formulas; SciPy
  finite-difference optimization replaces Torch autograd. The existing MIT
  Trotter/qDrift adaptation is reused with explicit bit-order conversion.
  The upstream closed Cartan-Lax optimizer is replaced by spectral SO(N) Cartan
  factorization. Closed CVD is not copied; molecular states can be prepared with
  open MPS/Isometry methods. See README.md and each coverage scope for differences.
  No unitarylab or unitarylab_algorithms distribution is imported or installed.

Direct runtime dependencies (transitive distributions are fixed in uv.lock):
  Qiskit 2.5.2 — Apache-2.0
  Qiskit Algorithms 0.4.0 — Apache-2.0
  PennyLane 0.45.1 — Apache-2.0
  quimb 1.15.0 — Apache-2.0
  PySCF 2.14.0 — Apache-2.0
